rl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104069564?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Wlkr123","id":104069564,"login":"Wlkr123","node_id":"U_kgDOBjP5vA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-operation/commit/1af704cee7a281fb61b068b89466f9287c5609ae","node_id":"C_kwDOUq-da9oAKDFhZjcwNGNlZTdhMjgxZmI2MWIwNjhiODk0NjZmOTI4N2M1NjA5YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-operation/commit/374b2d1bb27cf635e06d23abac57e6d7c5ba0e84","sha":"374b2d1bb27cf635e06d23abac57e6d7c5ba0e84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-operation/commits/374b2d1bb27cf635e06d23abac57e6d7c5ba0e84"}],"sha":"1af704cee7a281fb61b068b89466f9287c5609ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-operation/commits/1af704cee7a281fb61b068b89466f9287c5609ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104069564?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Wlkr123","id":104069564,"login":"Wlkr123","node_id":"U_kgDOBjP5vA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-operation/commits/374b2d1bb27cf635e06d23abac57e6d7c5ba0e84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T05:12:13Z","email":"104069564+Wlkr123@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Tuguldur"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T05:12:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(broadcast): HTML email rendering, realtime status, workflow broadcasts and module cleanup (#9445)\n\n* feat(email-editor): add shared Maily-based EmailEditor and render helper\n\nAdds a feature-agnostic EmailEditor component (frontend/libs/erxes-ui) wrapping\n@maily-to/core, and a matching renderEmailHtml() server-side helper\n(backend/core-api) wrapping @maily-to/render, so any consumer renders\nidentically to what it edits. Broadcast is the first consumer, wired in a\nfollow-up commit; email templates and automations can adopt the same\ncomponent later without copying code.\n\nPins @maily-to/core@0.3.7 and @maily-to/render@0.2.3 (both packages'' latest\nstable, pre-2.0.0-beta lines), per the Phase 0 feasibility findings.\n\n* feat(broadcast): add contentJson storage and Maily send/test-send path\n\nAdds an optional email.contentJson (Maily/Tiptap JSON) field alongside the\nexisting email.content (BlockNote JSON, kept as-is for old campaigns) -\nschema, GraphQL input, and validation. The send worker and\nengageMessageSendTestEmail now branch: contentJson present renders via the\nnew renderEmailHtml() + resolveEmailVariableValues() (per-recipient\npersonalization, matching the existing attribute-resolution behavior), with\nthe unsubscribe footer spliced onto Maily''s output since its renderer has no\nwrapper concept of its own. No contentJson falls through to the existing\nblocksToHtml() path untouched.\n\nFixes a real bug in engageMessageSendTestEmail while here: it previously ran\nBlockNote block JSON through the legacy {{ }} regex replacer and mailed the\nraw JSON as if it were HTML.\n\n* feat(broadcast): wire the Maily EmailEditor into the compose and preview flow\n\nBroadcast is the first consumer of the shared EmailEditor: compose (email.\ncontentJson field, personalization variables sourced from the existing\nfieldsCombinedByContentType query, same as the old attribute-insertion\nmenu) and the saved-record preview tab, which now renders Maily campaigns\nthrough a new engageMessageRenderPreview query so the preview always\nmatches what the render pipeline actually sends. Old BlockNote campaigns\n(content, no contentJson) keep rendering through the existing\nBlockEditor-readonly path unchanged.\n\nAlso fixes the resolveEmailVariableValues replacer type, missed in the\nprevious commit''s typecheck pass.\n\n* feat(broadcast): add a working test-send action\n\nengageMessageSendTestEmail existed on the backend but had no frontend call\nsite at all - clicking through to test a campaign wasn''t possible. Adds a\n\"Send test\" popover on the compose sheet''s final step (email method only)\nthat sends the current contentJson/subject/from through the mutation fixed\nin the previous backend commit.\n\nAlso fixes two stale ''email.content'' step-validation field references left\nover from before the contentJson switch.\n\n* feat(broadcast): add a broadcast-scoped email templates collection\n\nNew BroadcastEmailTemplates collection (name, description, contentJson) and\nGraphQL CRUD, scoped to broadcast rather than reusing the generic Template/\nTemplateCategory system (that one is built for multi-collection export/\ninstall bundles - product categories + products + UOMs - a poor structural\nfit for \"save one email body as a snippet\") or the automations-only\nAutomationEmailTemplates (unconnected to broadcast, still BlockNote-based).\n\n* feat(broadcast): wire save-as-template and insert-template into compose\n\n\"Save as template\" saves the current email.contentJson to the new\nBroadcastEmailTemplates collection. \"Insert template\" (next to the editor)\nreplaces the live document via the Tiptap editor instance''s\nsetContent(json, true) - the second arg matters, it''s what makes the\nprogrammatic replacement emit an update so the RHF-bound contentJson field\nstays in sync with what the user sees.\n\n* feat(broadcast): add email.previewText (inbox preview snippet)\n\nNew optional field, threaded through renderEmailHtml() (Maily''s own\nsetPreviewText(), which renders it as the standard hidden preheader) into\nthe send worker, engageMessageRenderPreview, and engageMessageSendTestEmail.\nPrep for the new compose layout''s \"Preview Text\" row.\n\n* feat(broadcast): rebuild email compose as a single-screen composer\n\nMatches the Maily playground composer''s structure (per reference screenshot):\ntop action bar (settings gear -> attachments, Preview Email, Copy HTML,\nSend Email as a plain-text action), then a Subject/From/To header block,\na Preview Text row, then the editor - replacing the old 2-step wizard for\nthe email method only. Messenger and notification are untouched and still\nuse the original step wizard (BroadcastStepsWizard, split out of\nBroadcastSteps).\n\nMapping decisions from the reference:\n- To row keeps the existing target-type/tag/brand/segment selector\n  components exactly, just repositioned behind a popover trigger instead of\n  its own wizard step.\n- Preview Email opens the rendered engageMessageRenderPreview HTML in a\n  dialog; Copy HTML renders the same and copies it to the clipboard;\n  Send Email is the existing test-send action, restyled as a plain-text\n  button per the reference (no filled background).\n- Settings gear holds Attachments, the one existing field with no natural\n  slot in the new compact header.\n- Campaign title moved into the sheet header as an editable input (the\n  reference has no separate title concept - Maily emails don''t have an\n  internal campaign name).\n\nAlso fixes i18n on every new/touched string here (broadcasts.json, en+mn) -\na gap in the previous composer pass that should have gone through\nreact-i18next from the start.\n\nBroadcastEmailMethod.tsx is now fully unreachable (verified via repo-wide\nsearch - zero remaining importers) and deleted.\n\n* fix(broadcast): fix composer spacing and header row alignment\n\nSheet.Content ships with zero padding by default (unlike Sheet.Header/\nSheet.Footer, both px-5) - the composer''s rows were rendering flush against\nthe sheet edges. Adds consistent px-5 to every content section, spans\nSeparators full-width between them, and gives the header rows more\nbreathing room (gap-5, larger vertical rhythm) matching \"generous spacing\"\nin the reference.\n\nAlso unifies the label column to w-24 across Subject/From/To/Preview Text\n(was w-20 for three of them, w-28 for Preview Text - misaligned), indents\nthe Reply-To reveal to align under the value column instead of the row\nstart, and drops the now-redundant p-10 on the editor''s own wrapper since\nthe composer applies that padding at the section level now.\n\n* chore(broadcast): delete unreachable dead code found during cleanup audit\n\nRan a repo-wide reference check across every file in the broadcast module\n(prompted by deleting BroadcastEmailMethod.tsx last commit) and found more\npre-existing orphans, unrelated to the Maily work - confirmed via `git diff\nmain` that none of this was touched before now:\n\n- BroadcastSheetActions.tsx: a stub that only ever rendered its own name\n- BroadcastSelectMember.tsx (SelectBroadcastMember) and the hook/contexts\n  only it used (useBroadcastMembers, BroadcastMemberContext,\n  BroadcastMemberInline, BroadcastMemberInlineContext): a from-user picker\n  that was apparently superseded by ui-modules'' generic SelectMember -\n  BroadcastMessengerMethod.tsx uses that one, confirmed before deleting.\n- The now-unused BROADCAST_MEMBERS query alongside it.\n\nLeft the backend engageMembers resolver alone - removing an API endpoint\nis a different, riskier call than removing a dead frontend consumer of it.\n\n* fix(broadcast): restore input padding and add horizontal padding to editor card\n\nThe row inputs (Subject/From/Preview Text) had px-0, stripping the base\nInput component''s default px-3 entirely to get the flush/muted look from\nthe reference - went too far and left the text jammed against the edge.\nRestored to px-2.\n\nThe editor''s white card also had py-8 but no horizontal padding at all -\nMaily''s own internal body wrapper carries a small ~16px cushion, but\nnothing beyond that. Added px-6 on the card itself.\n\n* fix(broadcast): fix a real regression in the aligned-sender From field\n\nAudit prompted by \"any logic not implemented from old broadcast left?\".\nFound a genuine functional regression, not just a display gap:\n\nWhen the org has an aligned/verified sender domain, the old\nBroadcastEmailMethod.tsx reused the field labeled \"Reply to\" to actually\npick *which* aligned address to send from (fromEmail, required) - a\npre-existing UX quirk (mislabeled field), but that field was always\nvisible in the grid. My composer rewrite put that same required field\nbehind the new Reply-To toggle, which is off by default - meaning an\naligned-sender org could submit without ever seeing the field that sets\nfromEmail. Split it apart: fromEmail''s sender picker is now always visible\nin the From row when aligned, and the toggle now only ever gates the\ngenuinely-optional email.replyTo field (non-aligned case).\n\nAlso found and fixed a real gap: the saved-record Preview tab\n(BroadcastEmailTabContent.tsx) never passed previewText into\nengageMessageRenderPreview, unlike every other render-preview call site\n(compose dialog, copy-HTML, test-send) - previewText silently wouldn''t\nshow there.\n\nAnd one more orphaned pre-existing stub found during the sweep:\nchooser/BroadcastChooser.tsx, zero references anywhere, predates this\nbranch (confirmed via git diff main).\n\n* fix(email-editor): sync contentJson on mount, not just on edit\n\nRoot cause of \"Preview Email shows an empty popup\": Tiptap''s onUpdate only\nfires on actual edits, never on initial mount, so a freshly-opened compose\nform had email.contentJson stuck at undefined until the user typed\nsomething. engageMessageRenderPreview requires contentJson: JSON! (non-\nnull), so previewing before typing anything sent an invalid GraphQL\nrequest - which failed with zero visible feedback, since neither the\npreview dialog nor the copy-HTML button read the query''s error at all.\n\nFixes both: EmailEditor now also syncs onCreate (an empty doc is still a\nvalid doc), and both call sites now surface query errors instead of\nsilently falling back to an empty string.\n\n* fix(broadcast): fix two bugs found by actually running the app\n\nLive-tested the full compose flow end to end (login, fill form, preview,\ncopy HTML, test send, save as template, insert template, save draft) with\nreal credentials against a running dev instance. Found two real bugs:\n\n1. BroadcastEmailComposer never wrapped EmailSenderScopeProvider - every\n   useSenderOptions() call in the new composer (From row, test-send,\n   preview, copy-HTML) silently defaulted to the ''transactional'' scope\n   instead of ''broadcast'', confirmed via direct network inspection (the\n   query was sending scope: \"transactional\" pre-fix, \"broadcast\" post-fix).\n   Same class of bug as the earlier BroadcastFromField regression, just a\n   layer higher - the whole composer never had the right scope context.\n\n2. BroadcastTargetPopover''s trigger text checked `targetCount` for\n   truthiness to decide whether to show \"Select recipients\" vs the count -\n   but a real selection can have a genuine count of 0 (an empty tag), and\n   0 is falsy, so the button kept showing \"Select recipients\" forever even\n   after a real, successful selection. Switched the check to\n   `targetIds.length`.\n\nAlso traced (not fixed, out of scope): this dev account''s AWS SES\ncredentials are invalid (\"InvalidClientTokenId\"), which cascades through\nApollo''s default errorPolicy discarding partial data into breaking\nalignedFrom resolution, test-send, and the sender-verification check in\ncheckCampaignDoc that Save & Draft depends on. Confirmed via direct GraphQL\ninspection that this is an infrastructure/credentials problem, not\nsomething in this codebase - every other part of the flow (compose,\npreview render, copy HTML, save-as-template, insert-template, the mutation\ncall itself) works correctly up to that AWS call.\n\n* fix(email-editor): remove Maily''s persistent menu bar and the duplicate card\n\nTwo things drifted from the reference (maily.to/playground):\n\n1. Maily renders a persistent Bold/Italic/Underline/Strike/clear-formatting/\n   alignment toolbar by default (its EditorMenuBar, a static row inside\n   #mly-editor, not a selection-triggered bubble menu - confirmed via DOM\n   inspection, it was always there regardless of selection). It''s controlled\n   by config.hasMenuBar, which nothing was setting. Now explicitly\n   config={{ hasMenuBar: false }} on the shared EmailEditor, so every\n   consumer gets the lean look - formatting still works via the bubble menu\n   on selection and the slash/@ menus, just not as a permanent bar.\n\n2. BroadcastEmailPreview wrapped the editor in its own bg-white/rounded-xl/\n   border/shadow card - but Maily''s own body wrapper already ships nearly\n   identical styling (mly:rounded mly:border mly:border-gray-200 mly:bg-\n   white). It was two nested cards. Removed erxes'' outer one, kept only the\n   scroll/layout wrapper.\n\n* fix(email-editor): add horizontal padding inside the editable text area\n\nAfter removing the outer card and Maily''s menu bar, the only inset left was\nMaily''s own body wrapper''s 16px. Added px-6 via config.contentClassName,\nwhich merges directly onto the ProseMirror contenteditable element''s own\nclass (confirmed via computed styles: padding-left/right now 24px on the\nactual input, not just a surrounding container).\n\n* fix(email-editor): remove Maily''s own body-wrapper border\n\nOne border was left after the earlier fixes: Maily''s native body wrapper\nships mly:border mly:border-gray-200 by default (separate from the outer\ncard erxes had added and already removed). Since Maily''s stylesheet loads\nafter erxes'' base styles, a plain border-none class risked losing the\ncascade depending on load order, so used Tailwind v4''s trailing-! important\nsyntax (border-none!, mt-0!) instead - confirmed via computed styles\n(border-width and margin-top both resolve to 0) rather than trusting it\nvisually.\n\n* fix(broadcast): increase composer sheet horizontal padding\n\npx-5 (20px) to px-8 (32px), applied consistently across Sheet.Header,\nevery Sheet.Content section, and Sheet.Footer via className overrides\n(cn() is tailwind-merge based, confirmed the override actually replaces\nrather than stacks with the shared Sheet component''s own px-5 default).\n\n* fix(email-editor): restore mouse interaction on Maily''s Tippy popups\n\nNot just \"can''t scroll the slash menu\" - confirmed via a real Playwright\nclick that mouse clicks on slash-menu items were completely broken too,\ntiming out as non-actionable.\n\nRoot cause: Maily''s slash/@/bubble menus are Tippy popups portaled\nstraight to document.body, outside Radix''s own Dialog/Sheet content tree.\nRadix sets body { pointer-events: none } while a Sheet is open (part of\nits scroll lock), and pointer-events inherits by default - so every Tippy\npopup silently inherited \"none\" too, since nothing re-enabled it the way\nRadix does for its own portaled content.\n\nFixed with a single scoped rule breaking the inheritance at the Tippy\nroot: [data-tippy-root] { pointer-events: auto }. Verified both directions\nlive: a real wheel event now moves scrollTop (was stuck at 0), and a real\nPlaywright click on a slash-menu item now succeeds and actually applies\n(confirmed visually - the placeholder rendered as a heading after the\nclick).\n\n* fix(email-editor): hide the mispositioned drag-handle tooltip\n\nReproduced and traced precisely: Maily wraps its drag-handle''s \"Add new\nnode\" hint in a Radix Tooltip (position:fixed Popper positioning), itself\nnested inside the handle''s own Tippy popup (transform-based positioning).\nA transform on an ancestor creates a new containing block for\nposition:fixed descendants per the CSS spec, so the Radix tooltip resolves\nits fixed position against the wrong origin - confirmed via\ndata-radix-popper-content-wrapper - and renders wherever that origin\nhappens to be, in this case outside the sheet entirely.\n\nThis is a real architecture collision inside Maily itself (two different\nfloating-UI positioning strategies nested inside each other), not\nsomething fixable by overriding position/transform CSS from the outside.\nSince the hint text isn''t needed for the handle to work - confirmed live\nthat both drag and click still function - hid it: [data-tippy-root]\n[data-radix-popper-content-wrapper] { display: none }, scoped narrowly\nenough to leave Radix tooltips/popovers used elsewhere in the app (outside\nany Tippy popup) untouched.\n\n* fix(email-editor): restore Show If popover on Section, Columns, and Repeat\n\nThe drag-handle tooltip fix''s hide-selector was too broad: it hid every\nRadix-Popper-in-Tippy popup, which also matched the \"Show If\" conditional\nvisibility popover on Section, Columns, and Repeat (Button''s Show If was\nunaffected since it''s implemented differently internally). Confirmed the\nidentical interaction works fine on the real maily.to/playground, proving\nthis was an erxes-integration regression, not a Maily bug.\n\nNarrow the selector to target only the broken tooltip using the z-index\nthat distinguishes it (50) from the Show If popover (9999), both\nconfirmed via direct DOM inspection. Verified live for Section, Columns,\nand Repeat with no regression on the drag-handle tooltip fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(email-editor): strip authoring comments and dead code from this branch\n\nCleanup pass across every commit on this branch: removes explanatory\ncomments added while building the Maily email editor and broadcast\ncomposer, and confirms (via cross-repo reference checks and\n--noUnusedLocals typechecks) there is no orphaned code left behind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(broadcast): drop brand targeting from the new composer''s target popover\n\nMerging origin/main pulled in an upstream change that removed brand-based\ncustomer targeting entirely (schema.ts''s targetType enum, the target-type\nselector, and BroadcastBrandStep.tsx itself are all gone there). Our new\nsingle-screen composer''s BroadcastTargetPopover still referenced the now\n-deleted BroadcastBrandStep and included ''brand'' in its type union, which\nbroke the typecheck post-merge. Bring it in line with segment/tag-only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in 0b16005 according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/9263\n\n* backend integration added\n\n* fix(broadcast): eliminate test-send from-address race condition\n\nBroadcastSendTestEmail relied on a separate component''s effect to have\nalready written the aligned sender address into shared form state before\nreading it - a timing race that surfaced as an intermittent \"from address\n... is missing\" error whenever the sender-options query hadn''t resolved\nyet. It now reads the aligned sender directly and disables the send\nbutton (with a \"Loading sender info...\" state) until that query settles,\nso a send attempt can no longer go out before the address is ready.\n\nAlso validates the test-send recipient is a single address, rejecting\ncomma-separated multiple recipients client-side with inline feedback\ninstead of only after a backend round-trip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert \"fix(broadcast): eliminate test-send from-address race condition\"\n\nThis reverts commit 06261dec8a8627eedede0a6b0880209195a77098.\n\n* fix(broadcast): eliminate email composer flicker and test-send race\n\nThe new-broadcast sheet briefly rendered the generic recipients wizard\nbefore swapping to the email composer, because open state was tracked\nseparately from the method URL param and resolved a render behind it.\nSheet open state is now derived directly from method.\n\nThe From field also flashed the manual address input before the\naligned-sender query resolved; it now shows a loading skeleton instead.\n\nReapplies the previously reverted fix for the intermittent \"from\naddress is missing\" error on Send Test Email: the button now waits\nfor sender options to load and reads the aligned sender directly\ninstead of relying on a sibling component to have already written it\ninto shared form state. Also adds inline validation (red outline +\nmessage) for invalid or multi-recipient test-send addresses, and\nturns the aligned-sender address into a button that explicitly fills\nthe from field.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(broadcast): enhance broadcast functionality with workflow support\n\n- Added new fields to BROADCAST_MESSAGE query: targetType, targetIds, targetCount, and workflowAutomationId.\n- Updated useBroadcastAdd and useBroadcastEdit hooks to handle workflowAutomationId.\n- Introduced useBroadcastEdit hook for editing broadcasts.\n- Modified useBroadcastForm to support workflow method and default values.\n- Extended broadcastSchema to include workflow method and its properties.\n- Implemented messageToFormValues utility to handle workflow data.\n- Updated prepareBroadcastVariables to include workflow data.\n- Integrated BroadcastEditSheet into BroadcastIndexPage for editing broadcasts.\n\nfeat(activity-logs): add CreatedVia functionality to activity logs\n\n- Introduced CreatedViaSuffix and CreatedViaSentence components to display the source of activity logs.\n- Updated DefaultActivitySentence to render CreatedViaSentence for activities created via automation.\n\nfeat(automations): implement template requirements for ticket and task modules\n\n- Added TicketTemplateRequirement and TaskTemplateRequirement components to handle prerequisites during template installation.\n- Updated TicketRemoteEntry and TaskRemoteEntry to include template requirements.\n\nchore: synchronize AGENTS.md files for frontline_ui, operation_ui, and sales_ui\n\n* feat(broadcast): send broadcast to a single contact from Contacts list\n\n* refactor(aiAgent): remove unused AI agent utility functions\n\n* feat(broadcast): add scheduling functionality and related utilities\n\n- Implemented `useBroadcastSchedule` hook for setting broadcast schedules.\n- Created `useBroadcastSchedulePreview` hook to preview scheduled broadcasts.\n- Added `useBroadcastScheduleRange` hook for managing schedule date ranges.\n- Introduced `broadcastListLayoutState` for persistent layout preferences.\n- Developed utility functions for handling broadcast methods and triggers.\n- Added calendar utilities for managing and displaying broadcast schedules.\n- Implemented campaign actions and status utilities for better campaign management.\n- Created recipient outcome utilities for handling broadcast recipient statuses.\n- Added schedule form utilities for managing broadcast scheduling forms.\n\n* ui improvement\n\n* feat(automations): enhance error handling and status reporting\n\n- Added `continueOnHttpError` option to OutgoingOptions to allow handling of non-2xx responses.\n- Improved segment loading logic to throw an error if a segment no longer exists.\n- Updated AutomationHistoryRecordTable to display a warning icon for actions that failed after completion.\n- Introduced ActionErrorPolicySection for configuring error handling policies directly within action forms.\n- Enhanced action history to include `handledFailureActionIds` for better tracking of failures.\n- Implemented new utility functions for managing action \"folks\" and branching logic.\n- Updated GraphQL queries and types to accommodate new fields related to action status and error handling.\n- Adjusted frontend components to reflect changes in action result handling, including skipped actions.\n\n* feat(automations): add requiresActor field to actions indicating ownership requirement\n\n- Introduced `requiresActor: true` in the action descriptors for ticket, task, project, and deal creation actions across frontline_api, operation_api, and sales_api plugins. This allows the automation builder to determine if the created records will belong to a specific user.\n- Updated AGENTS.md files to document the changes and their implications.\n- Enhanced automation execution logic to include ownership details, ensuring that records are created on behalf of the correct user.\n- Added new components and hooks in the frontend to manage automation ownership, including the ability to hand over ownership and display owner information in the UI.\n- Updated GraphQL queries and types to support the new ownership features and ensure proper data handling for approval requests related to ownership changes.\n\n* feat(email-templates): add document block functionality to email editor\n\n- Implemented `useEmailDocumentBlock` hook to manage document selection in the email editor.\n- Created `EmailDocumentPlaceholder` extension for rendering document placeholders in the email content.\n- Updated email templates hook to support cursor-based pagination and search functionality.\n- Introduced `emailTemplatesLayoutState` for persistent layout state management.\n- Enhanced settings breadcrumbs to support action buttons.\n- Added `EmailPreviewDeviceToggle` for switching between desktop and mobile previews.\n- Refactored email editor components to improve structure and usability, including the removal of deprecated product card functionality.\n- Added background color customization for email tables.\n- Created `SettingsDetailHeader` component for improved settings page navigation.\n\n* Refactor code structure for improved readability and maintainability\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: FazeTea <byrjvkhln.a@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: deepsource-autofix[bot] <62050782+deepsource-autofix[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"14d1f9da05b5d825ca5e829935259735d7150970","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-operation/git/trees/14d1f9da05b5d825ca5e829935259735d7150970"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-operation/git/commits/374b2d1bb27cf635e06d23abac57e6d7c5ba0e84","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","