//api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-sales/commit/151e32a0a065122e7c50a0aa6168abad1395cc5b","node_id":"C_kwDOUq-fi9oAKDE1MWUzMmEwYTA2NTEyMmU3YzUwYTBhYTYxNjhhYmFkMTM5NWNjNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-sales/commit/4ffe29662d0ec6d7445bd46f2b96b24a62616bba","sha":"4ffe29662d0ec6d7445bd46f2b96b24a62616bba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-sales/commits/4ffe29662d0ec6d7445bd46f2b96b24a62616bba"}],"sha":"151e32a0a065122e7c50a0aa6168abad1395cc5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-sales/commits/151e32a0a065122e7c50a0aa6168abad1395cc5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180429884?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Khuslen122/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Khuslen122/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Khuslen122/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Khuslen122/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Khuslen122","id":180429884,"login":"Khuslen122","node_id":"U_kgDOCsEkPA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Khuslen122/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Khuslen122/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Khuslen122/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Khuslen122/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Khuslen122/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Khuslen122","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-sales/commits/4ffe29662d0ec6d7445bd46f2b96b24a62616bba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T10:50:33Z","email":"huslens1027@gmail.com","name":"Khuslen122"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T10:50:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/sales deal detail revamp (#8764)\n\n* feat(sales): rebuild deal detail as an inline chip layout\n\nRework the deal detail to match the task detail: an editable title, a single\nwrapping row of inline chips instead of the two-column labelled grid, then\ndescription, attachments and the activity feed in one centered column.\n\nChips compose each shared select''s Provider/Value/Content around a local\n`Combobox.TriggerBase` (bordered, no chevron) the way operation_ui builds its\ntask chips, so the shared select roots stay untouched.\n\nAlso fixes several bugs found while testing:\n\n- Multi-selects (departments, branches, tags) appended to their local selected\n  list without deduping by _id, so a badge refetch grew the array and the\n  trigger showed a stale count until reload. Dedupe, switch to functional state\n  updates so parallel badge callbacks don''t clobber each other, and count from\n  the value prop rather than the cached objects.\n- Long department/branch titles were clipped mid-word inside a width-capped\n  trigger; badges now shrink (min-w-0) so the title ellipsises with a tooltip.\n- The deal title is debounce-saved, so a pending edit could land on the next\n  deal after switching records in the sheet. Key the field by deal id and skip\n  values already sent.\n- Every blur re-sent the description, logging a duplicate \"changed description\"\n  activity row each time the editor lost focus.\n- Re-picking the same broker type cleared the already chosen broker.\n- The overview tab did not pass dealCustomActivities, so sales-specific\n  activity rows fell back to the generic renderer there.\n\nAdds a deal note composer modeled on frontline''s message input (scoped\nmod+enter, mentions, permission gate) and the missing broker-type/broker and\nnote locale keys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sales): stop deal detail drafts leaking between records\n\nReview pass over the deal detail rework.\n\nThe sheet reuses one component tree across deals, so anything holding an\nunsaved draft carried over when the user switched records:\n\n- The title is debounce-saved, so a pending rename could resolve against the\n  next deal''s id.\n- The description keeps its pending value in refs, which only initialise on\n  mount, so blurring the field on a freshly opened deal could write the\n  previous deal''s body.\n- The note composer keeps unsent editor content, which would post to whichever\n  deal was open when Send was pressed.\n\nKey the overview subtree by deal id so all three reset together, and key the\nactivity tab''s composer the same way.\n\nAlso:\n\n- The title field adopted every incoming deal.name, including the echo of its\n  own in-flight save, which snapped the input back and dropped keystrokes typed\n  meanwhile. Ignore a value we already sent.\n- Attachment add/remove relied on useDealsEdit defaulting _id from the\n  board-card atom, which is never set when the sheet is opened from a\n  salesItemId URL — the mutation went out with a null id. Thread the deal id\n  through the attachment provider instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(sales): refine deal detail activity experience\n\n* fix(sales): address deal detail review findings\n\n* feat(sales): refine deal detail actions and document printing\n\n* fix(sales): address deal action sonar findings\n\n* fix(sales): stabilize deal detail selects and printing\n\n* refactor(sales): consolidate deal detail activity UI\n\n* test(sales): cover optimistic deal field updates\n\n* fix(sales): address review findings\n\n* chore(sales): remove optimistic field test\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Anu-Ujin <ujinka44@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac05b67240fbb4070452e08e21ff13e62de886d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-sales/git/trees/ac05b67240fbb4070452e08e21ff13e62de886d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-sales/git/commits/4ffe29662d0ec6d7445bd46f2b96b24a62616bba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-sales/commit/4ffe29662d0ec6d7445bd46f2b96b24a62616bba","node_id":"C_kwDOUq-fi9oAKDRmZmUyOTY2MmQwZWM2ZDc0NDViZDQ2ZjJiOTZiMjRhNjI2MTZiYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugi