n":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-tourism/commit/f55419be56eeba03230a23f7849ffdbdafb2f6fa","node_id":"C_kwDOUq-gQNoAKGY1NTQxOWJlNTZlZWJhMDMyMzBhMjNmNzg0OWZmZGJkYWZiMmY2ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-tourism/commit/0c0ad2eef3afd9cf0218a0ee27a0a8934fad6a74","sha":"0c0ad2eef3afd9cf0218a0ee27a0a8934fad6a74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-tourism/commits/0c0ad2eef3afd9cf0218a0ee27a0a8934fad6a74"}],"sha":"f55419be56eeba03230a23f7849ffdbdafb2f6fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-tourism/commits/f55419be56eeba03230a23f7849ffdbdafb2f6fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104069564?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Wlkr123","id":104069564,"login":"Wlkr123","node_id":"U_kgDOBjP5vA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-tourism/commits/0c0ad2eef3afd9cf0218a0ee27a0a8934fad6a74/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-23T14:15:27Z","email":"104069564+Wlkr123@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Tuguldur"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-23T14:15:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Import export v3 (#6733)\n\n* feat(import-export): implement import functionality with progress tracking and error handling\n\n- Added import module with support for CSV and XLSX file uploads.\n- Implemented import progress tracking, including status updates and error handling.\n- Created GraphQL mutations and queries for starting, canceling, retrying, and resuming imports.\n- Developed UI components for import file selection and progress display.\n- Integrated error file generation for failed imports and provided download functionality.\n- Enhanced backend with new models, resolvers, and worker processes for handling import tasks.\n\n* feat(import-export): enhance import functionality with Azure and Google Cloud support\n\n- Added support for Azure Blob Storage and Google Cloud Storage in the import module.\n- Refactored import-related GraphQL queries and mutations to accommodate new storage options.\n- Updated file reading utilities to handle files from multiple cloud storage providers.\n- Improved error handling and progress tracking for import operations.\n- Streamlined import processing logic and enhanced worker configurations for better performance.\n\n* feat(import-export): implement export functionality with GraphQL support\n\n- Introduced export mutations and queries for handling data exports.\n- Added export progress tracking and status management.\n- Implemented export field selection and active exports management in the UI.\n- Enhanced import-export hooks to support export operations.\n- Updated types and utilities for better integration with the export process.\n- Refactored existing import functionality to align with new export features.\n\n* feat(activity-logs): add activity log components and GraphQL integration\n\n- Introduced new components for displaying and managing activity logs.\n- Implemented GraphQL queries and subscriptions for real-time activity log updates.\n- Enhanced hooks for fetching and managing activity log data.\n- Added utility types and context for better integration with the activity log system.\n- Refactored existing import-export functionality to support activity log features.\n\n* feat(import-export): enhance import notification system and UI components\n\n- Updated loadImportClass to include event dispatcher for notifications.\n- Added ImportNotificationContent component for displaying import status and details.\n- Introduced useImportNotificationData hook for managing import metadata.\n- Implemented PieChart component for visual representation of import progress.\n- Refactored ExportHistories to utilize PieChart for progress display.\n- Integrated new import notification into CoreNotificationContent.\n\n* fix(utils): remove unused import from utils.ts\n\n- Eliminated the unused ''random'' import from the utils module to clean up the codebase.\n\n* feat(activity-logs): enhance activity logging functionality across modules\n\n- Updated connection resolvers to include event dispatchers for user, department, branch, and position models.\n- Introduced activity log generation for customer, company, and product changes.\n- Added new utility functions for generating activity logs in user and product models.\n- Integrated activity log creation into user and product creation and update processes.\n- Enhanced GraphQL subscriptions and queries to support activity log retrieval.\n- Refactored existing components to utilize the new activity log features.\n\n* feat(activity-logs): enhance activity logging functionality across modules\n\n- Updated connection resolvers to include event dispatchers for user, department, branch, and position models.\n- Introduced activity log generation for customer, company, and product changes.\n- Added new utility functions for generating activity logs in user and organization modules.\n- Integrated activity log creation into user and product class methods.\n- Enhanced GraphQL subscriptions and queries to support activity log retrieval.\n- Refactored existing components to display activity logs in customer and member detail views.\n- Improved overall activity log handling and context management for better performance and usability.\n\n* chore(dependencies): update package.json and enhance activity log utility\n\n- Added new dependencies: @azure/storage-blob, @google-cloud/storage, aws-sdk, and exceljs to support additional functionalities.\n- Refactored activity log utility functions to improve regex pattern matching and removed unnecessary console logs.\n- Updated file upload hook to include file size validation with user notification for oversized files.\n\n* chore(dependencies): add new packages for file handling\n\n- Added dependencies: file-type and form-data to enhance file processing capabilities in the project.\n\n* fix(trpc): simplify input structure for createOrUpdateConfig mutation\n\n- Updated the input schema for the createOrUpdateConfig mutation to accept a more flexible data structure by removing specific type constraints.\n- Refactored TRPC context types to enhance clarity and maintainability, introducing CommonTRPCContext for shared properties.\n\n* fix(models): update Uoms logging to reflect bulkWrite action\n\n- Changed logging action from ''create'' to ''bulkWrite'' in Uoms model.\n- Updated log structure to include newUoms in the update description for better clarity on inserted records.\n\n* refactor(import): streamline import/export type imports\n\n- Removed redundant imports of TGetExportDataInput, TGetExportHeadersInput, and TGetImportHeadersInput from zodSchemas.\n- Consolidated type imports from erxes-api-shared/core-modules for improved clarity and maintainability.","tree":{"sha":"34ecc1436287ae365c3cd636eb2c4687cb532ebc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-tourism/git/trees/34ecc1436287ae365c3cd636eb2c4687cb532ebc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-tourism/git/commits/0c0ad2eef3afd9cf0218a0ee27a0a8934fad6a74","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-tourism/commit/0c0ad2eef3afd9cf0218a0ee27a0a8934fad6a74","node_id":"C_kwDOUq-gQNoAKDBjMGFkMmVlZjNhZmQ5Y2YwMjE4YTBlZTI3YTBhODkzNGZhZDZhNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-tourism/commit/e826b24984b5d654117721e1d629a014930d9484","sha":"e826b24984b5d654117721e1d629a014930d9484","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amaraa0404org/erxes-plugin-tourism/commits/e826b24984b5d654117721e1d629a014930d9484"}],"sha":"0c0