te_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SKY-NYT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SKY-NYT/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SKY-NYT","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nzibukaemmanuel/Achievement_and_utilization_tracking_system/commits/2b36819b69818aed5150fa446e4596c3dcf3c3c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:47:22Z","email":"Fiko8464@gmail.com","name":"Kofi Frimpong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:47:22Z","email":"Fiko8464@gmail.com","name":"Kofi Frimpong"},"message":"fix(configurations): show an empty-state illustration for the metrics table and surface failed global-metrics loads\n\nThe scoring-framework metrics table only ever rendered a plain\n\"No metrics yet\" text row, regardless of whether the list was\ngenuinely empty or the underlying global-metrics fetch had silently\nfailed. Swap the table for the shared auts-empty-state illustration\nwhen there are no metrics, matching the pattern already used on the\nGlobal Metrics page.\n\nGlobalMetricsService.load() also swallowed every failure via an empty\ncatch block, so a failed fetch (GraphQL partial error or a response\nshape mismatch) looked identical to a legitimate empty list, with no\ntoast and no log. It now surfaces an error toast on failure, matching\nthe error handling already used by this service''s loadTablePage().","tree":{"sha":"dea162f7977903fa08ba998bdac9aca212a509ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nzibukaemmanuel/Achievement_and_utilization_tracking_system/git/trees/dea162f7977903fa08ba998bdac9aca212a509ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nzibukaemmanuel/Achievement_and_utilization_tracking_system/git/commits/2b36819b69818aed5150fa446e4596c3dcf3c3c7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u