.github.com/users/JohnNooney/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commits/895e9eba6a46bc256682522552b6b864e4ccbf6a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:05:49Z","email":"71711553+JohnNooney@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Nooney"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:05:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(host): ‹ up a level inside Folders on mobile (#55) (#56)\n\n* feat(host): ‹ up a level inside Folders on mobile (#55)\n\nMobile library is push navigation — the sidebar Folder tree is hidden\nand tiles navigate in — but inside a Folder nothing took you back up.\nThe browse toolbar now shows the reader''s ‹ {parent} affordance inside\nFolders: it names the parent Folder (Documents at top level) and taps up\nthrough OpenDocument.openFolder, the same seam as tile navigation. It''s\nmobile-only; desktop keeps the tree and is unchanged.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(host): ‹ affordance waits for the Folder''s record (#55)\n\nReview found the unresolved-folder fallback collapsed to ''Documents'' —\non a deep link before the folders snapshot lands, the button offered a\nlevel-skipping root jump. The affordance now stays hidden until the\nbrowsed Folder resolves, and the parent-name fallback reads ''Folder''\n(the reader''s convention) rather than ''Documents''. The spec fake''s\nfolderById derives from the folders signal like the real store.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d9ee9a525705f0a27cb65afae7da7b947d1a638","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/git/trees/2d9ee9a525705f0a27cb65afae7da7b947d1a638"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/git/commits/895e9eba6a46bc256682522552b6b864e4ccbf6a","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d9ee9a525705f0a27cb65afae7da7b947d1a638\nparent 3d2551606d3c74b4430ddb0c081e2f3792d944d1\nauthor John Nooney <71711553+JohnNooney@users.noreply.github.com> 1790676349 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790676349 +0100\n\nfeat(host): ‹ up a level inside Folders on mobile (#55) (#56)\n\n* feat(host): ‹ up a level inside Folders on mobile (#55)\n\nMobile library is push navigation — the sidebar Folder tree is hidden\nand tiles navigate in — but inside a Folder nothing took you back up.\nThe browse toolbar now shows the reader''s ‹ {parent} affordance inside\nFolders: it names the parent Folder (Documents at top level) and taps up\nthrough OpenDocument.openFolder, the same seam as tile navigation. It''s\nmobile-only; desktop keeps the tree and is unchanged.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(host): ‹ affordance waits for the Folder''s record (#55)\n\nReview found the unresolved-folder fallback collapsed to ''Documents'' —\non a deep link before the folders snapshot lands, the button offered a\nlevel-skipping root jump. The affordance now stays hidden until the\nbrowsed Folder resolves, and the parent-name fallback reads ''Folder''\n(the reader''s convention) rather than ''Documents''. The spec fake''s\nfolderById derives from the folders signal like the real store.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.n