t":"2026-09-29T06:40:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commit/ef5c8cd6e723929796cd50a68d251f8ec2ddb58e","node_id":"C_kwDOUsm60NoAKGVmNWM4Y2Q2ZTcyMzkyOTc5NmNkNTBhNjhkMjUxZjhlYzJkZGI1OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commit/407dc5b074db6dc0e9aad954e4a92e65dbd9e5d5","sha":"407dc5b074db6dc0e9aad954e4a92e65dbd9e5d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commits/407dc5b074db6dc0e9aad954e4a92e65dbd9e5d5"}],"sha":"ef5c8cd6e723929796cd50a68d251f8ec2ddb58e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commits/ef5c8cd6e723929796cd50a68d251f8ec2ddb58e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71711553?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JohnNooney","id":71711553,"login":"JohnNooney","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNzExNTUz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commits/407dc5b074db6dc0e9aad954e4a92e65dbd9e5d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:05:45Z","email":"71711553+JohnNooney@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Nooney"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:05:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Session flow and Extraction Job orchestration across the Bus (#31) (#44)\n\n* feat: Session flow and Extraction Job orchestration across the Bus (#31)\n\nHost-side orchestration that makes Sessions and background Extraction Jobs\nreal per Bus v1, ADRs 0003/0008, and the lifecycle decided in #15:\n\n- ExtractionFlow (scoped to the signed-in data layer) owns the three flows:\n  INIT_SESSION follows the open Document (stored Extraction +\n  extractionState, fresh sessionId per send); the job queue''s feeders\n  (uploading→ready transitions, load re-queue for ready Documents with no\n  Extraction/failure, RETRY_EXTRACTION); and outcomes (persist success at\n  extractions/current, record failures on the Document, resend Session on\n  open-Document completion, background toasts).\n- HostBus replaces ExtractionJobs as the app''s handle on the adapter;\n  HostBusEvents delegates outcomes to the flow; new probe hooks\n  (jobStarted/jobFailedFor/retryRequested) let the app own every re-enqueue.\n- Successful candidates are validated at the adapter boundary —\n  isExtractionCandidate + document/job identity — so only valid Extractions\n  reach persistence; INVALID_EXTRACTION lands as a recorded failure.\n- DocumentRecord gains extractionFailure (never auto-requeued, cleared on\n  retry; \"running\" is never persisted).\n- Guest renders the full Session state matrix from #15: Analyze/Try-again\n  send RETRY_EXTRACTION, stored Extraction stays readable under queued/\n  running indicators and the failed re-analysis warning banner, and the ⋯\n  menu offers \"Re-analyze document\" (hidden on non-COMPLETE, disabled while\n  a job is in flight).\n- Library route loads lazily (loadComponent), breaking the\n  providers ↔ library import cycle that extraction-flow would otherwise\n  close at module-eval time.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(#31): code-review follow-ups — sessionId freshness, retry guard, failed state\n\n- Fresh sessionId on the GUEST_READY resend (both Host adapters + a\n  conformance assertion): a stale SESSION_ACK from the old Guest instance\n  must never satisfy the resent Session''s watchdog.\n- A failed job now sits in the runtime job state as ''failed'' instead of\n  being cleared — the open Session flips straight to the retry affordance\n  instead of flickering ''none'' until the failure record''s snapshot lands.\n- retryRequested no-ops while that Document''s job is queued/running —\n  RETRY_EXTRACTION can no longer double-enqueue.\n- \"Couldn''t save the Extraction\" — glossary wording.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(#31): strip undefined fields before persisting the Extraction\n\nThe Guest''s Zod validation emits optional contract fields\n(documentTypeLabel, statusExplanation, takeaway page) as own-undefined\nproperties; postMessage''s structured clone preserves them and Firestore\nrejects the write — job success was landing as a persist failure.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"dfe874b7382670e5db580e45c11fb0fd40c10bde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/git/trees/dfe874b7382670e5db580e45c11fb0fd40c10bde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/git/commits/407dc5b074db6dc0e9aad954e4a92e65dbd9e5d5","verification":{"payload":"tree dfe874b7382670e5db580e45c11fb0fd40c10bde\nparent e35558edf13d0e78b4152e2b6e915ff972362a03\nauthor John Nooney <71711553+JohnNooney@users.noreply.github.com> 1790661945 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790661945 +0100\n\nSession flow and Extraction Job orchestration across the Bus (#31) (#44)\n\n* feat: Session flow and Extraction Job orchestration across the Bus (#31)\n\nHost-side orchestration that makes Sessions and background Extraction Jobs\nreal per Bus v1, ADRs 0003/0008, and the lifecycle decided in #15:\n\n- ExtractionFlow (scoped to the signed-in data layer) owns the three flows:\n  INIT_SESSION follows the open Document (stored Extraction +\n  extractionState, fresh sessionId per send); the job queue''s feeders\n  (uploading→ready transitions, load re-queue for ready Documents with no\n  Extraction/failure, RETRY_EXTRACTION); and outcomes (persist success at\n  extractions/current, record failures on the Document, resend Session on\n  open-Document completion, background toasts).\n- HostBus replaces ExtractionJobs as the app''s handle on the adapter;\n  HostBusEvents delegates outcomes to the flow; new probe hooks\n  (jobStarted/jobFailedFor/retryRequested) let the app own every re-enqueue.\n- Successful candidates are validated at the adapter boundary —\n  isExtractionCandidate + document/job identity — so only valid Extractions\n  reach persistence; INVALID_EXTRACTION lands as a recorded failure.\n- DocumentRecord gains extractionFailure (never auto-requeued, cleared on\n  retry; \"running\" is never persisted).\n- Guest renders the full Session state matrix from #15: Analyze/Try-again\n  send RETRY_EXTRACTION, stored Extraction stays readable under queued/\n  running indicators and the failed re-analysis warning banner, and the ⋯\n  menu offers \"Re-analyze document\" (hidden on non-COMPLETE, disabled while\n  a job is in flight).\n- Library route loads lazily (loadComponent), breaking the\n  providers ↔ library import cycle that extraction-flow would otherwise\n  close at module-eval time.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(#31): code-review follow-ups — sessionId freshness, retry guard, failed state\n\n- Fresh sessionId on the GUEST_READY resend (both Host adapters + a\n  conformance assertion): a stale SESSION_ACK from the old Guest instance\n  must never satisfy the resent Session''s watchdog.\n- A failed job now sits in the runtime job state as ''failed'' instead of\n  being cleared — the open Session flips straight to the retry affordance\n  instead of flickering ''none'' until the failure record''s snapshot lands.\n- retryRequested no-ops while that Document''s job is queued/running —\n  RETRY_EXTRACTION can no longer double-enqueue.\n- \"Couldn''t save the Extraction\" — glossary wording.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(#31): strip undefined fields before persisting the Extraction\n\nThe Guest''s Zod validation emits optional contract fields\n(documentTypeLabel, statusExplanation, takeaway page) as own-undefined\nproperties; postMessage''s structured clone preserves them and Firestore\nrejects the write — job success was landing as a persist failure.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu1U5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA11kQAGrc9PPOsnpICm3ED49Klmz/\n6H9+igIKLo8cVKnbFAskzzKTW78yY4OyB6rcE17u2V8b8SpG7D8I8X5kCKLwzhu5\nzc8O0cyy8Y0oRUQPx5xyA4HP8XhS0rB7D8S3Lq3foZBll4rkKxsFAG0PAs+e6Kw8\nZhZ/fx0F2lE91/NMd63WsSvNjERScqstRnwS/CKTEws9z8qFCYFAQkfP1OHGJDTR\nsk13DqhqanI3JfjQeg/ThxkuwLs27LI5JP1wUJfYKuW6xGvMuUEt2cjRnAuioJXW\nX9o6Y4LMt8KzFGQjhWab55PtupbbCBcq+gLsyM2KGuEpZZO6lbdM/k53g3jwpW0a\nK1jJwUlw7sYrfo4IuFNVhGM3tINUpMpQCHH/EaE3HAa31g9Y1K/4dfxLXMKLOn6z\n8bolVt6o7MqakhCEl5pfQp/n8/MzlX6NzGDGl5nR5cyfR7RLt+AtjHqgvd7moAWe\noVirzr6fRNiyMoSrZFrPwFbb+aTxmQZTT3xF+4qiMV/sFRoK2+DRwa0v1dY1ajSl\n7/N2kW2Lwfz3P0GK/adQZF0x+fQV90pkkysJMi5ZDSsMiiokrAN7qX4X3aZR21Jr\nyKgJBCPQ176rtDu1eTeQVQHcm/yHKIbMZLrkaxoW0hyhGsFWr7m0s3YbksurMY+K\nkOIxocne9fN70/fH7dxB\n=vExS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T06:05:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commit/407dc5b074db6dc0e9aad954e4a92e65dbd9e5d5","node_id":"C_kwDOUsm60NoAKDQwN2RjNWIwNzRkYjZkYzBlOWFhZDk1NGU0YTkyZTY1ZGJkOWU1ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commit/e35558edf13d0e78b4152e2b6e915ff972362a03","sha":"e35558edf13d0e78b4152e2b6e915ff972362a03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commits/e35558edf13d0e78b4152e2b6e915ff972362a03"}],"sha":"407dc5b074db6dc0e9aad954e4a92e65dbd9e5d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commits/407dc5b074db6dc0e9aad954e4a92e65dbd9e5d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71711553?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JohnNooney","id":71711553,"login":"JohnNooney","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNzExNTUz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnNooney","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/commits/e35558edf13d0e78b4152e2b6e915ff972362a03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:20:29Z","email":"71711553+JohnNooney@users.noreply.github.com","name":"John Nooney"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:20:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Guest Extraction client: Gemini via AI Logic, schema validation, fake provider (#30) (#43)\n\n* Guest Extraction client: Gemini via AI Logic, schema validation, fake provider (#30)\n\nThe EXTRACT_DOCUMENT runner was a stub rejecting with AI_UNAVAILABLE.\nThis wires the real pipeline behind the provider seam:\n\n- extraction-schema: the #8 responseSchema (SchemaRequest subset) plus the\n  canonical Zod validator enforcing the rules the wire schema can''t —\n  required conditionals, word/char bounds, BCP 47, the five-CRITICAL cap.\n- gemini-provider: inline application/pdf bytes, structured output, one\n  repair pass carrying the invalid JSON + validation errors (no PDF\n  re-upload), then fail closed with INVALID_EXTRACTION; SDK/App Check/quota\n  failures map to the contract''s typed codes.\n- fake-provider: the seeded fixture Extractions byte-for-byte behind\n  VITE_FAKE_AI_PROVIDER (e2e CI sets it); unseeded Documents fall back to\n  the golden Bus fixture re-stamped with their documentId.\n- prompt: klartext-extraction-v1 verbatim from #8.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Move seeded Extraction fixtures into bus-contract; share enum literals\n\nReview fixes: the fake provider no longer reaches into scripts/ via a\ndeep relative import — the fixture JSON lives in packages/bus-contract\n(already the home of fixture data \"for tests and fake providers\"), the\nseeder reads the same file, and one as-const literal list per enum feeds\nboth the wire schema and the Zod validator so they can''t drift.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Document and ship the Storage bucket CORS config\n\nBrowser getBytes/upload calls hit firebasestorage.googleapis.com\ncross-origin; without a bucket CORS policy every non-emulator origin —\npreview channels and production — fails to read PDFs. The emulator\nignores CORS so nothing surfaced in dev/e2e. Hashed per-PR preview\nhostnames make an origin list unworkable, hence \"*\": rules and App\nCheck remain the access boundary.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Skip reCAPTCHA provider init in App Check debug mode\n\nThe SDK still calls provider.initialize() when the debug token is set —\nthe debug flag only swaps the token exchange. On localhost the Host''s\nreCAPTCHA Enterprise render then failed with \"Missing required\nparameters: sitekey\" (dev config carries no site key), and both apps\nloaded the reCAPTCHA script for nothing. A CustomProvider whose getToken\ncan never be called in debug mode keeps it out of dev/preview.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Serve fixture Extractions on preview channels\n\nThe baked App Check debug token makes the preview Guest''s Gemini path\ncallable by anyone who loads the channel — bounded by the #21 quotas but\na real spend exposure. The fake provider keeps previews deterministic\nand free; the real round-trip stays available in dev.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Use limited-use App Check tokens for Gemini + live verify spec\n\nfirebaseml (Vertex AI in Firebase) has replay protection ENFORCED on\nthis project — regular exchanged tokens are rejected by\nfirebasevertexai with 401 \"token is invalid\". getAI now requests a\nlimited-use token per call; valid whether or not protection is on.\n\nAlso adds the opt-in gemini-live spec (VERIFY_GEMINI=1) covering the\nacceptance criterion''s real round-trip: debug exchange, anonymous\nsign-in, real generateContent on a seeded fixture PDF. Verified\nagainst the live project (3248 tokens, valid candidate) after\nenabling aiplatform.googleapis.com, which the console''s AI Logic\nsetup did not enable; both gotchas are now in deployment.md.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Switch Gemini to the Developer API backend for the free tier\n\nGoogleAIBackend replaces VertexAIBackend — calls still flow through\nthe firebasevertexai gateway (same App Check path), but bill against\nthe Gemini Developer API free tier instead of Blaze Vertex. ADR 0007\nrevised: its gs:// rationale was already moot (inline bytes won) and\nno region-pinning requirement exists.\n\ngemini-2.5-flash is retired for new users on the Developer API, so\nEXTRACTION_MODEL moves to the backend-recommended gemini-3.8-flash;\nfixtures keep 2.5-flash as historical record data. Live verify now\nreaches the model service — it currently fails 429 because the\nproject''s Gemini Developer API prepayment credits are depleted, an\nAI Studio billing state resolved at ai.studio/projects, not in code.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix the live-verify invocation in the docs\n\npnpm --filter only matches package scripts, so `vitest` needs `exec`.\nVerified: the Developer API round-trip passes live (gemini-3.8-flash,\nvalid candidate, 1504 tokens).\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4a10f4515f44b89f13c0f332602aab30ec05c629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/git/trees/4a10f4515f44b89f13c0f332602aab30ec05c629"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JohnNooney/KlartextDMS/git/commits/e35558edf13d0e78b4152e2b6e915ff972362a03","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a10f4515f44b89f13c0f332602aab30ec05c629